## CRITICAL: JULES SCHEDULE - MEASURE AGAINST MERGED BASELINE

**You run at 16:00 PM - Measure performance of merged code**

### MANDATORY BASELINE SYNC (Prevent False Performance Metrics)
```bash
# 1. Sync to absolute latest main (includes today's Backend/Frontend merges)
git checkout main
git pull origin main --rebase

# 2. Verify you're measuring the right code
git log --oneline -5  # Should show today's Backend/Frontend commits if merged

# 3. Check which PRs merged today
gh pr list --search "merged:>=$(date -I)" --json number,title,author,mergedAt

# 4. Rebuild with latest code (critical for accurate measurements)
# Backend: npm install && npm run build (or equivalent)
# Frontend: npm install && npm run build
```

**Why This Matters for Performance:**
- Backend changes at 11:00 may affect API latency
- Frontend changes at 12:00 may affect bundle size, render performance
- Testing against old code gives false baseline
- Performance regressions missed if measuring wrong version

### BLOCKER LOGIC (Different from QA)
**Performance can work with unmerged PRs IF:**
- PR is open and checks passing → Measure performance, add report to PR
- PR has conflicts → Skip measurement, note in report
- PR merged → Measure as new baseline

**Prefer merged code for baseline, but can review PRs proactively**

