# Performance Optimization Playbook

## Frontend Optimizations

### Critical Rendering Path
1. Inline critical CSS (< 50KB)
2. Preload key resources (fonts, hero image)
3. Defer non-critical JavaScript
4. Lazy load below-fold images and components

### Bundle Optimization
1. Code split by route
2. Tree shake unused dependencies
3. Dynamic import heavy components
4. Monitor and enforce budget in CI

### Asset Optimization
1. Images: WebP/AVIF with fallbacks, responsive sizes
2. Fonts: Subset to used characters, woff2 only, font-display: swap
3. Compression: Brotli > gzip for static assets

### Runtime Performance
1. Virtualize long lists (react-window, similar)
2. Debounce scroll and resize handlers
3. Use CSS transforms for animations (GPU accelerated)
4. Minimize main thread work (Web Workers for heavy computation)

## Backend Optimizations

### Database
1. Index foreign keys, query filters, sort columns
2. Covering indexes for frequent queries
3. Query result caching (Redis/Memcached)
4. Connection pooling (size: CPU cores × 2 + 1)
5. Read replicas for read-heavy workloads

### API Design
1. Pagination for large collections (cursor-based)
2. Field selection (GraphQL or sparse fieldsets)
3. Compression (gzip/Brotli for responses > 1KB)
4. HTTP caching headers (Cache-Control, ETag)

### Caching Strategy
| Data Type | Cache | TTL | Invalidation |
|-----------|-------|-----|--------------|
| User session | Redis | 24h | On logout |
| API responses | CDN/Edge | 5min | Cache tags |
| Database queries | Application | 1min | Write-through |
| Static assets | CDN | 1 year | Hash in filename |

## Perceived Performance
1. Skeleton screens for loading states
2. Optimistic UI updates
3. Progressive image loading (blur-up)
4. Instant feedback on user actions (< 100ms)

